WEBVTT

00:39.460 --> 00:42.510
I dreamed of that time again...

00:44.540 --> 00:47.560
I still can't let go
of my unfulfilled dreams...

00:51.950 --> 00:53.400
Is the game still going on?

00:57.940 --> 00:59.190
As I recall, that guy...

01:00.600 --> 01:03.710
The Best Rookie, Fay.

01:04.080 --> 01:05.840
That means...
Right here!

01:09.070 --> 01:13.030
The gods smile at those
who make their own miracles!

01:16.210 --> 01:18.600
'Let the god bring down the god.'

01:19.280 --> 01:24.020
This was your strategy, Uroboros.

01:24.750 --> 01:28.480
I... I never knew such
stirring gameplay existed!

01:29.560 --> 01:30.470
I've decided!

01:30.860 --> 01:35.410
I, Nel Reckless, vow to offer up
my very life to you!

02:05.440 --> 02:07.110
GODS' GAMES WE PLAY

02:08.480 --> 02:13.740
GODS' GAMES WE PLAY

03:07.630 --> 03:09.190
PLAYER.05: WORLD GAMES TOUR

03:09.190 --> 03:10.420
What?!

03:10.420 --> 03:12.730
Why can't we dive right away?!

03:12.730 --> 03:16.530
We've formed a team
with Pearl as our official member!

03:19.320 --> 03:21.270
Now, please take a look at this.

03:23.890 --> 03:24.620
DIVINE GATE I-IV | EXPECTED WAIT TIME FOR DIVE,
TEAMS ON WAITLIST

03:24.620 --> 03:25.890
What is this?

03:25.890 --> 03:27.890
It's the status of the Dive Request

03:27.890 --> 03:30.730
for the Divine Gate that our branch is keeping,

03:30.730 --> 03:32.990
but they are all booked up,

03:32.990 --> 03:35.510
and the earliest you can wait is a month.

03:35.510 --> 03:37.450
Huh? How can that be?!

03:37.770 --> 03:39.600
I'm sorry to say,

03:39.600 --> 03:43.490
but the reason is Fay and you,
Lady Leshea.

03:44.620 --> 03:48.110
The first feat in human history,
the defeat of Uroboros,

03:48.110 --> 03:50.170
was the best stimulant

03:50.170 --> 03:54.410
to make all apostles in the Ruin Branch
submit their applications to dive all at once.

03:54.410 --> 03:56.940
I see. I understand now.

03:59.860 --> 04:01.530
We're going to the Dive Center.

04:01.530 --> 04:03.420
Huh? Why are we going?

04:03.420 --> 04:06.230
We're going to steal the Divine Gate.
By force.

04:06.850 --> 04:10.310
What are you talking about?!
Please don't do that!

04:10.310 --> 04:12.320
Ah, wait, Lady Leshea!

04:12.320 --> 04:14.380
Hold on tight!

04:14.380 --> 04:17.050
Please stop!

04:17.050 --> 04:20.320
My arse is worn out and flattened!

04:20.320 --> 04:22.410
It's dangerous if it continues.

04:22.760 --> 04:25.710
Leshea, who has game withdrawal symptoms,
might go berserk.

04:27.390 --> 04:28.950
Do you have any good ideas?

04:29.380 --> 04:32.130
Something that we can try right away.

04:32.130 --> 04:33.450
I do.

04:33.450 --> 04:34.650
Really?!

04:34.650 --> 04:37.430
Eyes on the monitors again, everyone.

04:39.550 --> 04:41.550
PROPOSAL FOR WGT (WORLD GAMES TOUR)

04:41.550 --> 04:43.950
World Games Tour?

04:57.500 --> 04:59.110
I have nothing

04:59.440 --> 05:01.560
but respect for the old apostles.

05:02.070 --> 05:06.950
After they retired from the military,
they used their Arise powers to guard the city

05:07.500 --> 05:12.160
and gradually explore and develop
an area in the outside world.

05:13.110 --> 05:19.460
Oh, by the way, we were invited to
the Sacred Spring City, Mal-ra, right?

05:19.460 --> 05:19.960
Huh?

05:20.420 --> 05:21.090
Yeah.

05:22.220 --> 05:23.340
What is this?

05:23.340 --> 05:27.810
It's like how athletes are invited to play
tournaments around the world.

05:27.810 --> 05:29.870
From the day after you defeated Uroboros,

05:29.870 --> 05:34.120
we started getting a lot of requests
to play in their games.

05:34.120 --> 05:35.140
Why?

05:35.520 --> 05:38.780
An apostle who wins a game against
a god that is difficult to defeat

05:38.780 --> 05:41.280
is considered a hero by the world.

05:43.820 --> 05:45.240
SACRED SPRING CITY, MAL-RA

05:45.830 --> 05:47.240
VOLCANO CITY, VOLDANRA

05:47.830 --> 05:49.250
OCEAN CITY, FISSHARA

05:49.250 --> 05:52.250
So far, the cities where we've
received offers are these cities.

05:52.580 --> 05:59.130
I, Pearl, feel honored that you've entrusted me
to choose the city for our tour!

05:59.490 --> 06:00.890
Well, then...

06:01.550 --> 06:03.130
There!

06:05.050 --> 06:06.050
SACRED SPRING CITY, MAL-RA

06:06.050 --> 06:07.430
SACRED SPRING CITY, MAL-RA
Will there be apostles

06:07.430 --> 06:09.590
from the Mal-ra Branch?

06:09.590 --> 06:10.770
Probably.

06:11.370 --> 06:13.250
I wonder what kind of apostles they are.

06:26.450 --> 06:30.330
SACRED SPRING CITY, MAL-RA

06:33.160 --> 06:34.880
We made it!

06:34.880 --> 06:36.130
We're finally here!

06:36.130 --> 06:38.750
What is the most famous local game here?

06:38.750 --> 06:41.160
We need to visit the game shops first!

06:41.160 --> 06:42.760
Let's go, Fay!

06:43.090 --> 06:45.560
We've got to visit
the Mal-ra branch office first.

06:45.560 --> 06:46.740
Say, guys...

06:47.470 --> 06:49.820
Who is that person?

06:50.810 --> 06:53.770
A WARM WELCOME TO MASTER FAY AND HIS TEAM
WELCOME TO OUR CITY

06:53.770 --> 06:56.730
She's really suspicious.

06:56.730 --> 06:59.420
I don't understand it either.

06:59.420 --> 07:01.820
I've got a bad feeling about this.

07:04.630 --> 07:07.070
Ah, those people over there, could it be...!

07:08.460 --> 07:09.730
Let's run.

07:17.610 --> 07:18.570
What?!

07:19.920 --> 07:22.980
A superhuman with enhanced
physical abilities...

07:23.780 --> 07:25.760
Are you an apostle?

07:26.250 --> 07:27.830
Allow me to introduce myself.

07:27.830 --> 07:32.130
My name is Nel Reckless, a former apostle
serving in the Sacred Spring City of Mal-ra.

07:32.600 --> 07:34.310
Former apostle?

07:34.310 --> 07:35.310
Master Fay!

07:35.310 --> 07:38.050
I want you to make me your woman!

07:40.340 --> 07:40.910
Huh?

07:42.730 --> 07:43.790
Ah.

07:44.880 --> 07:47.180
I mean, I want you to make me
your subordinate.

07:47.180 --> 07:48.900
And that's how you tell me?!

07:48.900 --> 07:49.920
Master Fay,

07:53.990 --> 07:57.360
after seeing the stream of you
fighting Uroboros, I was convinced.

07:57.360 --> 08:00.580
You are the only master
I was destined to serve!

08:00.870 --> 08:03.410
Please make me your subordinate!

08:03.790 --> 08:07.680
No, wait, "subordinate" or "master"
is such an exaggeration...

08:07.680 --> 08:09.360
It's not exaggerating!

08:09.360 --> 08:12.610
I will cook, wash, iron your clothes,
and do anything else!

08:12.610 --> 08:14.500
I-If you want,

08:14.500 --> 08:17.140
I-I'll even wash your back in the bath...

08:17.140 --> 08:19.570
You shouldn't say that in public!

08:19.570 --> 08:21.730
What is going on here?

08:22.280 --> 08:23.360
Hey, Leshea...

08:23.360 --> 08:26.470
Fay, to have such thoughts when you
have a being like me with you...

08:26.470 --> 08:30.280
I can't continue to defend a man
who asks a strange girl

08:30.280 --> 08:32.630
to wash his back in the bathtub.

08:32.630 --> 08:34.320
But you should defend me!

08:34.320 --> 08:35.240
Master Fay!

08:36.080 --> 08:37.390
I beg you!

08:42.160 --> 08:44.140
Please make me your subordinate!

08:46.760 --> 08:47.660
Huh?

08:53.050 --> 08:55.130
Please wait, Master Fay!

08:55.510 --> 08:56.510
Watch out!

09:06.690 --> 09:09.650
MOMENT REVERSAL:
PUSHED AWAY ANY ENERGIES OR MASS

09:17.430 --> 09:20.140
Oh, crap! I didn't mean to!

09:20.140 --> 09:22.780
Are you okay, Mr. Driver?!

09:31.420 --> 09:33.130
I think we lost her.

09:33.530 --> 09:36.680
W-Who was that girl?

09:36.680 --> 09:38.660
I don't know.

09:38.660 --> 09:41.420
But I think it's the right thing to do
to run away from her.

09:45.270 --> 09:48.040
Oh, is that Undine the Water Spirit?

09:48.040 --> 09:49.780
Are they the apostles from Ruin?

09:49.780 --> 09:52.230
The apostles who defeated Uroboros?

09:52.720 --> 09:53.830
Really?!

09:53.830 --> 09:55.150
You guys...

09:59.520 --> 10:00.960
Are you guys by any chance...

10:02.360 --> 10:04.520
A pervert!

10:05.540 --> 10:09.000
Mr. Security Guard, he's a pervert!

10:09.000 --> 10:10.710
I'm not a pervert.

10:10.710 --> 10:13.260
He's definitely a pervert!

10:13.260 --> 10:15.260
I'm the chief secretary here.

10:15.260 --> 10:15.930
Eh?

10:16.380 --> 10:17.040
Huh?

10:17.920 --> 10:21.280
Welcome to the Mal-ra branch
of the Arcane Court.

10:21.800 --> 10:24.940
I'm the chief secretary, Baleggar Ions.

10:26.020 --> 10:29.020
IS IT NOT TIME YET?
GODS' GAMES WE PLAY

10:39.170 --> 10:42.960
Umm, why are we taking the stairs?

10:43.470 --> 10:46.220
Because the chief secretary's office
is on the 8th floor.

10:46.220 --> 10:51.600
No, I mean... There was
an elevator right there.

10:51.600 --> 10:53.800
This is better for your health.

11:02.060 --> 11:05.730
Now, about the World Games Tour,

11:05.730 --> 11:08.980
the main event is the gods' game
to be played in three days.

11:09.430 --> 11:13.860
We have already rented out a sports stadium
in a city as a cheering venue.

11:14.320 --> 11:18.030
The 10,000 seats are booked
to watch you play.

11:18.030 --> 11:21.240
10,000 people?! You sold every ticket?!

11:21.240 --> 11:25.140
The people of Mal-ra
will be cheering for you.

11:26.330 --> 11:28.210
Oh, no, I'm not sure about that...

11:28.210 --> 11:30.890
And one other event

11:30.890 --> 11:34.760
is the friendly match to foster friendship
between us that will be held tomorrow.

11:35.190 --> 11:37.300
I hope you'll agree.

11:37.300 --> 11:38.910
If it's okay with us,

11:38.910 --> 11:43.020
it would be a great opportunity
to enjoy those two games.

11:43.380 --> 11:45.750
We have been inundated
with volunteers.

11:46.480 --> 11:49.690
They wanted to test their strength
with a former god, Lady Leolesha,

11:49.690 --> 11:53.130
and the best rookie, Fay.

11:53.130 --> 11:55.240
That's it.

11:55.240 --> 11:57.700
What? Does that mean I'm in?

11:57.700 --> 11:59.800
I mean, of course!

11:59.800 --> 12:02.870
I did defeat the undefeated god, right?

12:02.870 --> 12:06.160
I must be getting attention from
apostles all over the world.

12:09.390 --> 12:11.140
Why the total silence?!

12:11.140 --> 12:14.460
Wait, Chief Secretary!
What about my popularity?!

12:22.510 --> 12:26.120
These are commemorative photos
from last year's World Games Tour.

12:27.730 --> 12:31.490
All of them are apostles who participated
as guests from other cities.

12:31.490 --> 12:34.650
Oh, what's this one?
That's a very unusual color.

12:34.650 --> 12:38.420
Oh, the black outfit
is the best team in this branch.

12:38.870 --> 12:40.240
The gold embroidery means...

12:40.240 --> 12:41.390
Headquarters.

12:42.480 --> 12:46.720
Only members of Arcane Court headquarters
are allowed to wear that golden embroidery.

12:46.720 --> 12:48.500
I haven't seen those uniforms before.

12:52.670 --> 12:56.460
The blue trim... Are they the guests
from the Ruin branch office?

12:59.120 --> 13:01.820
Oh, Dax. That's just like you.

13:01.820 --> 13:05.770
I should have known you would want
to greet them before the event.

13:05.770 --> 13:08.350
Allow me to introduce him.
This guy is...

13:08.350 --> 13:11.600
I'm Dax.
Dax Gear Scimitar.

13:12.790 --> 13:15.390
I've heard a lot about you guys.

13:15.390 --> 13:17.510
"You guys"?

13:17.510 --> 13:20.170
Watch your mouth, Dax!
This person is a former god!

13:20.170 --> 13:22.330
I'm not inclined to offer
any special treatment.

13:22.950 --> 13:26.720
All I care about is whether
they're good at the game or not.

13:26.720 --> 13:27.830
That's all.

13:28.290 --> 13:30.780
Well, that's good to hear.

13:30.780 --> 13:34.160
I like people like you
who only have eyes for games.

13:34.840 --> 13:37.270
Umm, Chief Secretary...

13:37.270 --> 13:40.120
He's wearing a black outfit...

13:40.120 --> 13:41.970
Exactly what you think it does.

13:42.340 --> 13:44.250
A year ago, as a rookie,

13:44.250 --> 13:47.170
he established his own team
in the fastest time on record.

13:47.170 --> 13:50.130
And they took victory against
the gods in their first game.

13:51.560 --> 13:54.130
His current record is
three wins and one loss.

13:54.580 --> 13:57.400
He is now the representative of our branch.

13:57.400 --> 13:59.650
A-Amazing...

14:00.010 --> 14:01.460
He's just like Fay...

14:02.560 --> 14:04.040
Fay Theo Philus.

14:12.210 --> 14:13.430
I knew it.

14:13.840 --> 14:18.170
We were destined to meet after all.

14:18.980 --> 14:19.670
Sorry?

14:20.020 --> 14:22.780
The battle against Titan and Uroboros.

14:22.780 --> 14:24.820
You deserve praise for your performance.

14:25.340 --> 14:27.390
Huh? Ah, thank you.

14:27.390 --> 14:29.350
Therefore, I say unto you:

14:29.350 --> 14:32.480
Come to join my team,
Tempest Cruisers!

14:33.870 --> 14:35.070
Ah...

14:35.070 --> 14:39.380
I'm gathering the best rookies
from all over the world,

14:39.380 --> 14:42.950
and we're going to form
the strongest team in history,

14:43.290 --> 14:45.710
aiming to get Clear in gods' game!

14:49.180 --> 14:53.590
And Fay,
you are the final piece that I seek!

14:53.590 --> 14:55.090
Come with me!

14:56.900 --> 15:01.380
I'm sorry to turn you down,
but we're here for the World Games Tour.

15:02.040 --> 15:03.680
Not to join anyone's team.

15:04.470 --> 15:05.330
I see.

15:05.330 --> 15:08.240
Eh? Huh? Are you fine with that?

15:08.240 --> 15:09.890
My business here is finished.

15:13.330 --> 15:16.850
There are a lot of interesting
people in this branch.

15:17.320 --> 15:21.060
Especially since that didn't look like
the face of a guy who'd given up.

15:24.970 --> 15:27.030
I just wanted to show
you two something.

15:27.030 --> 15:30.870
Since we're going to be teaming up with
apostles from the Mar-la in a couple of days,

15:30.870 --> 15:33.750
I want to see how they play.

15:34.270 --> 15:36.210
And I just happened to spot this...

15:37.460 --> 15:41.170
Ah! I remember seeing this girl before!

15:41.170 --> 15:42.290
That's right.

15:42.290 --> 15:45.410
She is Nel Reckless, the girl
who asked me to be my subordinate

15:45.410 --> 15:47.050
when we first met her.

15:47.780 --> 15:52.100
I looked into it...
She had retired just a month ago.

15:52.480 --> 15:55.060
Her final record was
three wins and three losses.

15:55.060 --> 15:57.590
Not a great number,

15:58.020 --> 16:01.090
but she's a very good player.
I'm not saying that to flatter her.

16:01.980 --> 16:04.440
She is able to follow her captain's
orders without a hitch

16:04.770 --> 16:07.130
and backs up her friends
at every opportunity.

16:07.970 --> 16:08.820
They found him!

16:12.730 --> 16:13.740
Cra...

16:15.420 --> 16:19.370
The three of us should push the switch,
and a decoy should attract the god...

16:19.370 --> 16:21.460
We needed four people...

16:22.050 --> 16:23.370
It's a dead end.

16:23.370 --> 16:29.150
We've been found, and god
is in full surveillance mode.

16:32.810 --> 16:34.060
We give up.

16:34.060 --> 16:36.140
Hold on, Captain...

16:36.140 --> 16:38.140
This game isn't over yet!

16:39.150 --> 16:41.350
By majority vote,

16:41.350 --> 16:44.860
this game, "God Has Fallen," is over.

16:44.860 --> 16:48.070
Three of us are still standing!

16:48.540 --> 16:49.780
Please!

16:50.070 --> 16:52.450
I don't want it to end this way!

16:57.430 --> 17:00.250
Was it really a good idea
for them to give up?

17:00.550 --> 17:03.670
The name of the game is "God Has Fallen."

17:03.670 --> 17:06.550
I'm curious about the shape of that god.

17:06.550 --> 17:07.710
Fay...

17:08.610 --> 17:12.020
Nel is basically my opposite, right?

17:12.430 --> 17:16.020
I was so fed up with my team's
defeat due to my own failure

17:16.020 --> 17:19.490
that I decided to retire.

17:19.490 --> 17:21.990
But Nel was the opposite.

17:22.810 --> 17:27.110
I guess she retired with the feeling
that she had unfinished business.

17:27.110 --> 17:28.620
Could be.

17:28.620 --> 17:31.010
She should have told us
what was going on.

17:31.010 --> 17:33.820
Now I look like the bad guy
for running away from her.

17:39.720 --> 17:41.890
Is that Mr. Chief Secretary Baleggar?

17:42.250 --> 17:44.430
This is room service.

17:44.880 --> 17:46.240
Yes, please.

17:47.210 --> 17:49.170
Y-You're...

17:49.910 --> 17:52.430
I'm not suspicious.

17:52.430 --> 17:53.960
You're Nel, right?

17:55.640 --> 17:58.390
Nel? What are you doing?

17:58.390 --> 18:02.350
W-Who is that?
T-What's not my name.

18:02.670 --> 18:04.190
No, I can tell by your voice.

18:04.190 --> 18:06.320
And the color of your hair.

18:08.600 --> 18:10.570
C-Crap!

18:11.230 --> 18:12.280
Bye!

18:12.280 --> 18:13.740
Ah, hey!

18:15.940 --> 18:19.140
I just wanted to talk to her.

18:27.130 --> 18:30.470
Why did I run away?

18:31.130 --> 18:32.480
That's not like you.

18:33.610 --> 18:36.050
To wind up with your tail
between your legs.

18:36.830 --> 18:37.770
Dax...

18:37.770 --> 18:42.270
Nel, two years ago,
we were assigned together.

18:42.270 --> 18:45.620
Everybody wondered which one of us
would come out on top in this generation.

18:45.620 --> 18:46.970
That's what they said.

18:47.310 --> 18:51.190
But I survived, and you retired.

18:51.190 --> 18:54.910
What's the difference between us?
Talent? Skill?

18:56.410 --> 18:58.030
You can call it whatever you like.

18:58.510 --> 18:59.490
It's the team.

19:01.110 --> 19:04.360
You were unlucky.
You had bad luck with your teammates.

19:06.580 --> 19:09.720
Use your skills and become
our team's analyst!

19:09.720 --> 19:11.250
Come join my team!

19:12.080 --> 19:15.590
That's useless.
I want to be on Master Fay's team.

19:16.080 --> 19:18.400
I'm not going to join anywhere else.

19:18.400 --> 19:20.320
If you insist,

19:20.930 --> 19:23.270
let's make a bet with me,

19:23.270 --> 19:25.030
on the friendly match tomorrow.

19:27.190 --> 19:28.300
Interesting.

19:28.890 --> 19:31.320
I bet Master Fay will win.

19:37.360 --> 19:39.740
That's a lot of cheers.

19:39.740 --> 19:44.020
I wonder what kind of games
we will play in such a big venue!

19:47.740 --> 19:48.680
Nel?

19:51.560 --> 19:52.830
I made it in time...

19:55.120 --> 19:58.170
Master Fay, you probably know by now

19:58.170 --> 20:00.600
that your opponent
for this friendly match is Dax.

20:00.600 --> 20:04.720
He definitely has a real deal
when it comes to games.

20:04.720 --> 20:07.440
Even someone like you
would find it difficult to avoid it.

20:08.300 --> 20:10.590
But...! But please win!

20:10.590 --> 20:12.480
Otherwise...

20:16.430 --> 20:18.010
Is it time already?

20:18.010 --> 20:20.130
A-Anyway, I'm counting on you!

20:22.010 --> 20:24.590
I'll be cheering for you
from the spectator seats!

20:29.120 --> 20:33.210
That human Nel,
did she come to cheer us on?

20:33.730 --> 20:35.280
Guess so.

20:35.670 --> 20:38.420
It's nice to know someone's
going to cheer us on.

21:03.460 --> 21:06.220
This is a Pride Match between two cities.

21:06.220 --> 21:09.870
But I haven't a shred of interest
in defending my city's honor!

21:10.770 --> 21:13.050
As an athlete of the game,

21:13.050 --> 21:16.280
I'm here to pit my spirit
against yours in battle!

21:19.380 --> 21:20.220
What?

21:22.280 --> 21:25.890
No, I hope you'll take this as a compliment.

21:25.890 --> 21:29.510
You're hot-blooded. I thought
you were a cool-blooded guy.

21:29.850 --> 21:31.490
It depends on my opponent.

21:31.490 --> 21:35.360
Therefore, show me something
that makes my soul burn bright!

21:35.670 --> 21:38.980
Let's get to the game selection.
To make everything fair,

21:38.980 --> 21:41.710
one game will be chosen at random
from the thousands of games

21:41.710 --> 21:43.870
set up in this stadium.

21:46.580 --> 21:49.790
Operator, start up the chosen game!

21:53.600 --> 21:55.710
Augmented reality image?

22:01.620 --> 22:02.770
This is...

